Q5. DEMONSTRATE AND RESOLVE A GIT MERGE CONFLICT
Project: GitMergeConflict
Create a repository and a shared file:
1. cd ~/Desktop
2. mkdir GitMergeConflict
3. cd GitMergeConflict
4. printf "Project status: Initial\n" > status.txt
5. git init
6. git branch -M main
7. git add status.txt
8. git commit -m "Initial commit"
Create a feature branch and change the same line:
9. git switch -c feature
10. printf "Project status: Updated by feature branch\n" > status.txt
11. git add status.txt
12. git commit -m "Update status on feature branch"
Return to main and change that SAME line differently:
13. git switch main
14. printf "Project status: Updated by main branch\n" > status.txt
15. git add status.txt
16. git commit -m "Update status on main branch"
Merge feature into main to produce a conflict:
17. git merge feature
Git should report a merge conflict in status.txt.
Open the conflicted file:
18. notepad status.txt
Resolve the conflict manually in Notepad.
Delete all conflict marker lines (<<<<<<<, =======, and >>>>>>>).
Keep the final content you want, for example:
Project status: Final resolved version
Save and close Notepad.
Mark the conflict as resolved and complete the merge:
19. git status
20. git add status.txt
21. git status
22. git commit -m "Resolve merge conflict"
Verify the result:
23. git log --oneline --graph --all
24. git status
Expected final status: "nothing to commit, working tree clean".